@codex review

Please review the full refactor in this PR, including the cleanup at `88602d27260c33b6efa0c6b8acf5d708b6c80bc8`. Focus on correctness, unnecessary complexity, invocation/AST ownership, scheduler cancellation and joining, jobserver token/descriptor lifetime, freshness semantics, generation leases and immutable-object publication, and potential performance regressions.

The cleanup passes all 28 normal checks, all 17 ASan/UBSan checks (session ownership also with LeakSanitizer), both 858-case snapshot profiles, and all 27 external GNU incremental scenarios. The fresh paired performance campaign is running; the first attempt hit the workspace inode limit and is retained as incomplete evidence. Previous performance evidence is explicitly tied to the earlier runtime. Real PC qualification remains unrun, and the PR remains draft.

@codex review

Please review the updated head `20580cd3819e83b86a2be576b0f9798d2aad0f79`, including the fix for discussion_r4433451269. The deferred double-colon `$?` probe now preserves phony/logical prerequisites and low-resolution timestamps while retaining the saved-graph helper format. The new direct/build/legacy regression tests and full correctness suite pass; the remaining portable and sanitizer checks are running.

Performance remains explicitly unqualified for the cleanup head: the retained 88602d2 campaign passed 55/60 cells, with five timing failures. A same-environment fd7573b-to-88602d2 control found no statistically supported regression but wide intervals. A larger, predeclared fixed-head campaign with explicit CPU affinity will run after correctness validation. Real PC qualification remains unrun, and this PR stays draft.

@codex review

Please review `5302d4f989608f090b0eb32ca4cbbb5e6a50d16f`, especially the final cleanup in Ninja emission. Silent phony `@:` recipes with the default `/bin/sh -c`, no command environment changes, no deferred runtime evaluation and no explicit recursive prefix now retain their phony dependency edges without launching a shell. Echoed commands, custom shells/flags, exports and deferred evaluation still execute. The new regression test passes before and after the change and checks repeated rebuilds through an existing phony file, prerequisites, inherited export effects, custom shells/flags and visible commands. Both builds pass; full normal/sanitizer validation is running.

The prior `20580cd` code passed all correctness checks and all three CI workflows, but its strict performance campaign passed 57/60 cells. Main and large-graph cells all passed; remaining failures were near-parity parallel execution and 0.7–0.9% slower 2,000-recipe generated launch cases. A shorter shell environment guard was tested and rejected because it did not improve performance. The final runtime will receive a fresh predeclared campaign with unchanged thresholds. The PR stays draft; real PC qualification remains unrun.

@codex review

Please review d4dca5fd9a282a596d867e16781863fbc2665471, particularly generation publication. Fresh graphs no longer create/sync an empty legacy snapshot when no standalone artifacts exist. Existing public aliases with the exact desired target remain unchanged; new aliases use atomic creation, and replacement of different entries still uses atomic rename. The root/parent/artifact durability barriers are retained. The legacy migration test now removes the current pointer so it exercises first migration, and passes before and after the change. All 14 architecture tests pass on the exact new binary.

This addresses unnecessary publication work found after the prior runtime's fixed precision extension confirmed a 3.3% small end-to-end clean regression (59/60 cells passed). The new binary receives a fresh predeclared campaign, checking that clean case first at 1,001 pairs. No thresholds were relaxed, and earlier failures remain retained. Full validation is pending for this new runtime; the PR remains draft.

@codex review

Please review fdff3e56aecf8dbfbde1cc55253347b101c0db42. The ordinary Ninja freshness guard now checks output existence in its existing shell before spawning the native timestamp helper. A missing output cannot be current; existing outputs still use the native probe, and a nonempty intermediate-consumer proof retains the original path. The guard remains stable across first and later builds. The existing current/stale-output regression test now also checks rebuilding a deleted output.

The diagnostic binary passes all 192 correctness cases in both profiles and the Make compatibility suite. A syscall trace confirms 32→0 freshness-probe processes in the 32-output clean fixture, with correct outputs. The preceding publication-only commit still failed its 1,001-pair clean gate at +2.1%; it remains recorded as failed. This new runtime receives the same predeclared full qualification and unchanged thresholds. The PR remains draft while validation runs.
